{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CdyCaZM29MUawhhiRtr1U","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"# Fix Plan\n\n## 1. **Declare the numeric contract in the mapper**\n   - **Where:** `golden/mapper.ts`\n   - **Change:** Round the `irr` field to **9 decimal places** (or 1e-9 precision) before serialization, matching the product spec's declared tolerance for projected amounts.\n   - **Concrete code pattern:**\n     ```typescript\n     irr: Math.round(irr * 1e9) / 1e9\n     ```\n\n## 2. **Regenerate the baseline on Node 20**\n   - **Where:** Local machine or CI environment pinned to Node 20\n   - **Command:** Re-run the snapshot writer to freeze `golden/projections.json` with the rounded `irr` values\n   - **Rationale:** The baseline must reflect the normalized contract, not raw FP noise; Node 20 is the documented freezing environment\n\n## 3. **Verify the fix on both supported majors**\n   - **Run:** Full CI suite (Node 20 and Node 22)\n   - **Expected outcome:** Both jobs pass; the 1e-14 to 2e-13 deltas absorbed by the 1e-9 rounding, no behavioral regression because genuine IRR changes would exceed the tolerance\n\n## Rationale\nThe deltas (1e-14 to 2e-13) are environmental FP noise, not behavioral bugs. The fix lives in the comparator layer (mapper), not production code. The declared tolerance (1e-9) justifies the rounding and makes the gate portable by construction, not by accident."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":689,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":371,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}}
